WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.860
- Well, the hour is almost up,

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:04.470
but let's get to one last story
that might make you smile.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.932
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:05.932 --> 00:00:08.220
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.740
For over a century, people
across Latin America

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.360
have enjoyed the game Loteria.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.550
It's basically a version of Bingo

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:17.340
in which each square is
represented by an image.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.680
Not long ago, a Los
Angeles man was looking

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.740
at the old set that he had
played as a kid in Guatemala

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.120
and he realized that those images

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.240
really didn't represent the
younger generation of Latinos.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.970
So, he decided to invest his life savings

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.890
into making a modern set.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.650
It's become a huge hit and
something we want to celebrate

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.150
this Hispanic Heritage Month.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:37.800
Everybody, let's welcome the creator

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.200
of Millennial Loteria, Mike.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.033
What's up, Mike?

00:00:42.612 --> 00:00:45.150
- Hola, Kelly. Hi, everyone.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:46.680
- Hola. So, okay, great to meet you.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.540
Can you explain the game a little more

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.980
and how you updated it?

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.480
- Yeah, so the great thing about Loteria,

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.620
it is not just a game,

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:53.910
it is a tradition, like you say,

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:56.370
that was, has been played
for countless generations.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.890
And one of the things that I
saw is that, as Millennials,

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:01.290
we grew up playing this
game with, like, our family,

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:02.370
our abuelas.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:05.970
But as time went on, we kind
of put down the Loteria set

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:08.040
and started picking up our cell phones

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.370
and our video games and,
you know, watching TV

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.440
and kind of not playing that game anymore.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.990
And so, I'm a firm believer that Loteria

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:19.020
doesn't belong in, like, a
Latin American history museum.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.910
It belongs in your living room.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:22.980
So, I decided that I wanted to update it

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:26.100
to reflect modern Latino
Millennials nowadays.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.620
So, for instance, the old Loteria

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.190
it had a a picture of la
dama, which is the lady.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.740
And so, I decided I wanted to update that

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.840
to make sure that Millennials
felt more represented.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.280
So, it's 2022.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.980
She's no longer just la
dama, she's now la feminist.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.245
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:42.245 --> 00:01:43.560
- And so, I started putting
these updates online,

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.150
and it went viral.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.970
So, it was very exciting
for me to see, you know,

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:51.330
people reacting to me updating
a card to be el hipster,

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:56.330
el global warming, la selfie,
la student debt, el pride.

00:01:57.037 --> 00:02:01.680
- La student debt. This is awesome.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.450
So, why do you think
that this is resonating

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.850
with younger people, and
how do older Latinos react

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:06.780
to the modern version?

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.220
It's so funny.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:09.053
- Well, thank you.

00:02:09.053 --> 00:02:09.886
I mean, you know, we've sold

00:02:09.886 --> 00:02:11.940
over half a million sets to date.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.258
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:02:13.258 --> 00:02:14.970
- So I'm celebrating
that younger generations

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:18.900
have felt really, you know,
represented in this game.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.360
And it's also a fun game
for older people, too.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.310
I mean, there's always gonna
be Boomers who are like,

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.260
Millennials are ruining everything again,

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.607
Millennials ruining Loteria,

00:02:26.607 --> 00:02:28.590
but I think it's also a fun game

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:32.130
to bring generations together
and to show how, you know,

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.450
there's things that unite us.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:34.440
At the end of the day,

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.719
regardless of what the
images of the cards are,

00:02:36.719 --> 00:02:39.690
Loteria is a game that
brings people together,

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.850
that creates fond memories with people.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.318
And I'm really passionate about having

00:02:43.318 --> 00:02:46.050
not only this game
celebrated around the world,

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:48.330
but having other cultures embrace, too,

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.730
how fun it is to play this game.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:51.900
- Absolutely. I'm down.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.240
I love game night, and
that is awesome and funny.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.730
You did a great job with
your life savings, brother.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.260
Thank you so much, Mike.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.183
I'm liking your post right now.

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:01.866
(bell dings)

00:03:01.866 --> 00:03:03.120
- [Mike] Thanks a lot.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:03.953
- And that's not all.

00:03:03.953 --> 00:03:06.360
Our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.100
the go-to pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.280
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like you, sir,

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.620
making a difference for
their culture and community.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.720
So, they'll be writing
you a check for $1000.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:16.570
How's that sound?

00:03:17.731 --> 00:03:19.470
- Wow! Thank you so much.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:20.910
Thank you, thank you so much, Kelly.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:22.983
That's amazing. I'm super excited.

